  {question:"GST was introduced in India from:",options:{A:"April 1, 2017",B:"July 1, 2017",C:"January 1, 2018",D:"April 1, 2018"},answer:"B",topic:"GST",difficulty:"easy",explanation:"GST was implemented from July 1, 2017, subsuming multiple indirect taxes like excise duty, service tax, VAT, etc."},
  {question:"The threshold limit for GST registration for goods is:",options:{A:"Rs 20 lakh",B:"Rs 40 lakh",C:"Rs 10 lakh",D:"Rs 50 lakh"},answer:"B",topic:"GST",difficulty:"medium",explanation:"For goods, the threshold for GST registration is Rs 40 lakh (Rs 20 lakh for special category states). For services, it is Rs 20 lakh."},
  {question:"Input Tax Credit (ITC) under GST means:",options:{A:"Credit of output tax",B:"Credit of input tax paid on purchases",C:"Refund of tax",D:"Exemption from tax"},answer:"B",topic:"GST",difficulty:"easy",explanation:"ITC means the credit of input tax (CGST/SGST/IGST) paid on inputs/input services/capital goods, which can be used to pay output tax."},
  {question:"Under the Income Tax Act, PAN stands for:",options:{A:"Permanent Account Number",B:"Permanent Assessment Number",C:"Primary Account Number",D:"Personal Account Number"},answer:"A",topic:"Income Tax",difficulty:"easy",explanation:"PAN (Permanent Account Number) is a 10-character alphanumeric identifier issued under Section 139A of the Income Tax Act."},
  {question:"Section 194Q deals with TDS on:",options:{A:"Salary",B:"Purchase of goods exceeding Rs 50 lakh",C:"Rent",D:"Professional fees"},answer:"B",topic:"TDS",difficulty:"medium",explanation:"Section 194Q requires buyer to deduct TDS at 0.1% on purchase of goods exceeding Rs 50 lakh in a financial year."}
